  "description": "SlideRule is the spec contract: the fluent builder and reified rule model an architecture spec is written against. It is the one package a spec project references. A spec declares layers, rules and scopes. A rule is either the law (Enforce) or a ratchet over a counted baseline (Migrate). A scope either fails a new reference into it (Quarantine) or only warns when a change touches it (Caution). Checking and rendering come from the sliderule tool (SlideRule.Cli) or the xUnit adapter (SlideRule.Xunit). The package carries a Roslyn analyzer that reports a spec's bad string literals as compiler warnings while the spec is written. It also carries a completion provider that offers the referenced projects' namespaces and type names inside the editor. This package is netstandard2.0 with zero dependencies, so a spec project can target anything from net48 up.",
